
================================================================================================
1. Rev 1.3 headline claims vs arithmetic (config A: 24,576 MACs at 3.2 GHz)
================================================================================================
Dense INT8 peak        :   157.3 TOPS   (24,576 MAC x 2 ops x 3.2 GHz)
2:4-sparse peak        :   314.6 TOPS   (industry-comparable number)
Claimed 1258 TOPS      : needs a sparsity factor of 8.00x  -> this is the 8:1 number
Claimed 2516 TOPS INT4 : dense INT4 is   314.6 TOPS; 2516 again needs 8:1
DRAM 512-bit x 6400 MT/s =  409.6 GB/s raw  (claim 400 GB/s: consistent)
Dense efficiency @3.2 GHz, 100% util, Tj 105 C : 2.09 TOPS/W (claim 15-30 TOPS/W needs 7.2-14.3x -> sparse units again)
Power at 3.2 GHz, 100% util, Tj 105 C          :  75.2 W  (claim: 40-50 W typical, 70-90 W peak)
Leakage of an un-gated die at Tj 125 C          :  14.5 W  (claim: 1-5 W always-on mode)

================================================================================================
2. Thermal: maximum dissipation for Tj_max = 125 C by cooling method and ambient
================================================================================================
Cooling (R_theta_ja, C/W)                Ta=65 C   Ta=85 C  Ta=105 C  Ta=125 C
Passive, sealed ECU (2.5)                  24.0W     16.0W      8.0W      0.0W
Passive, large finned housing (1.2)        50.0W     33.3W     16.7W      0.0W
Forced air (0.6)                          100.0W     66.7W     33.3W      0.0W
Cold plate / liquid (0.25)                240.0W    160.0W     80.0W      0.0W
Verdict: 70-90 W (or 40-50 W) 'passive cooling' is impossible above ~65 C ambient; at 125 C nothing dissipates.

